  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I couldn't find a past ticket reporting this same problem: a default-terminal handoff for an MSIX (Store) PowerShell Preview whose process runs from the versioned WindowsApps package path, which doesn't match the generated profile's app execution alias path. The tickets I was shown are about other issues. terminal#10228 is about the wrong profile being used on handoff in general and was closed as a duplicate of #9458, which was not provided. terminal#20333 is about the MSIX PowerShell Preview profile not showing up at all. Until this is tracked, keep using your workaround of a hidden profile whose commandline is the real package path, and update it after each PowerShell Preview update. Please file this as a new issue and include your proposal to resolve app execution aliases (IO_REPARSE_TAG_APPEXECLINK) or match by package family name during profile matching.\"}",
